<title>UK: Bacob sets $150 million three-year bond.</title>
<headline>Bacob sets $150 million three-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced</p>
<p>by joint lead managers Yamaichi International Europe (books) and</p>
<p>Bacob Bank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BACOB OVERSEAS BANK</p>
<p> AMT    $150 MLN	COUPON     6.50	MATURITY    31.JUL.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.10    PAY DATE    30.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.375     REOFFER    99.95     SPREAD	+25 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	A2	  LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  A	   DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  BELGIAN   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.225     SELL CONC  1.15	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF MTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
